From b5186e6bea748e54015e046be46b4dc178a5800f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minpeter <62207008+minpeter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:32:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 108/112] sunxi: h713: the HY320 - clear 0x058c0000, the video
 plane shows

The HY320's LogoRegData.bin leaves 0x058c0000 (mirrored at 0x058c1000) at
0x10000040 from its prologue, and its DE group ends without touching it
again. The L018's file -- the same 1920x1080 dual-port panel class --
closes its DE group with 0x058c0000 = 0 (record +0x22dc).

Bit 28 of that word blanks the video plane at the mixer and nothing else:
with it set, a frame the firmware has processed reaches the panel block's
probes (0x051c0144, 0x051c0304, the histogram at 0x051c0380..0x03fc) as
white and the wall stays black, while the RGB channel shows normally and a
half-transparent RGB overlay shows black where the video should be.

Measured on the owner's unit, 01.11.2026, by eye at the wall:
- 0x10000040 (the file's value): video black, under the "ADT-3 2024"
  display firmware and under the HY310's (16c74a28...) alike;
- 0x00000040: video shown; 0x10000000: black;
- the L018's whole LogoRegData.bin: video shown under both firmwares;
- this change with the board's own files, the stock kernel module and
  nothing else: colour bars and motion on the video plane.

Under CONFIG_H713_BOARD_HY320 only: the other ADT-3 family boards have
not been measured.
---
 arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
index 95e8eaa16e5..280ff476473 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/h713_mips.c
@@ -6605,6 +6605,26 @@ static int h713_disp_run(ulong blob, u32 project, bool skip_hdcp_wait,
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_H713_BOARD_HY320
+	/*
+	 * The HY320's LogoRegData.bin ("ADT-3 2024" family) leaves
+	 * 0x058c0000 (and its mirror at 0x058c1000) at 0x10000040 from the
+	 * prologue, and its DE group ends there. The L018's file -- the same
+	 * 1920x1080 dual-port class of panel -- closes its DE group with
+	 * 0x058c0000 = 0 (record +0x22dc). Bit 28 of that word blanks the
+	 * video plane at the mixer and nothing else: with it set, a frame the
+	 * firmware has processed reaches the panel block's own probes
+	 * (0x051c0144, 0x051c0304) and the wall stays black, while the RGB
+	 * channel shows normally. Measured on the owner's unit 01.11.2026:
+	 * 0x10000000 alone blanks the video, 0x00000040 alone does not, and
+	 * the L018's word 0 shows it under both display firmwares.
+	 */
+	writel(0, 0x058c0000);
+	writel(0, 0x058c1000);
+	printf("H713 panel: HY320 - 0x058c0000 cleared as the L018's DE group "
+	       "does (bit 28 blanks the video plane)\n");
+#endif
+
 	if (stock_panel_power) {
 		ret = h713_disp_stock_panel_power();
 		if (ret)
